# Cline Rules for FinanControl

## AI-Powered Project Knowledge Base

Before performing any task on this project, always read and reference the AI folder for complete project context. This ensures all code changes align with the established architecture, conventions, and patterns.

### Required Reading (Always Load First)

When starting any task, read these skill files from `AI/skills/`:

| Priority | File | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| 1 | `AI/skills/project-overview.md` | Understand the app's purpose, features, and entry points |
| 2 | `AI/skills/architecture.md` | MVVM + Repository pattern, package structure, data flow |
| 3 | `AI/skills/tech-stack.md` | Libraries, versions, dependencies, test libs, and CI/CD |
| 4 | `AI/skills/coding-conventions.md` | Kotlin patterns, Kotlin DSL, ViewBinding, coroutines, repos, naming, testing |
| 5 | `AI/skills/database-schema.md` | Room entities, DAOs, and relationships |
| 6 | `AI/skills/navigation-flow.md` | Nav graph, Safe Args, and dialog flow |
| 7 | `AI/skills/ui-components.md` | Fragments, adapters, dialogs, and FancyChart |
| 8 | `AI/skills/firebase-integration.md` | Firebase services and configuration |
| 9 | `AI/skills/strings-localization.md` | String resources and Spanish localization |
| 10 | `AI/skills/cicd-github-actions.md` | CI/CD workflows, signing config, GitHub Releases |

### Agent Role Definitions

When you need to act in a specific role, load the corresponding agent file from `AI/agents/`:

| Agent File | Use When |
|------------|----------|
| `AI/agents/android-developer.md` | General development, bug fixes, or implementing features |
| `AI/agents/feature-builder.md` | Building a complete new feature end-to-end |
| `AI/agents/code-reviewer.md` | Reviewing code for correctness and conventions |
| `AI/agents/test-writer.md` | Writing unit tests with MockK + Page Object pattern |

### Additional Rule: READ AI FOLDER FIRST

**CRITICAL**: If the `AI/` directory exists and you haven't read it yet during this conversation, always read all files in `AI/skills/` before making any code changes. This is non-negotiable — the AI folder contains the ground truth for how this project is structured and built.

### Project Quick Facts

- **App**: FinanControl — Personal finance tracking Android app
- **Package**: `com.locotoDevTeam.financontrol`
- **Language**: Kotlin 2.0.21 (JVM target 1.8), with some Java chart classes
- **Build System**: Gradle 8.13 with **Kotlin DSL** (`.gradle.kts`) + **Version Catalog** (`libs.versions.toml`)
- **Architecture**: MVVM + Repository with Room, LiveData, ViewModel, Navigation 2.8.7, ViewBinding, **Hilt DI (Dagger 2.52)**
- **AGP**: 8.13.2 — **compileSdk 36**, **targetSdk 36**, minSdk 21
- **JDK**: 21 (Android Studio bundled locally, Temurin 21 on CI)
- **Database**: Room 2.4.1 with `Category` and `Income` entities
- **Firebase**: Analytics, Auth, Crashlytics, Cloud Messaging (BOM 29.1.0)
- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions — `build.yml` (debug APK + tests on push/PR) and `release.yml` (signed release APK on `v*` tags)
- **Testing**: JUnit 4.13.2, MockK 1.13.13, Kotlinx Coroutines Test 1.8.1, Arch Core Testing 2.2.0

### Key Conventions

#### Build
- Build files are **Kotlin DSL** (`.kts`), not Groovy — use `=` for properties, `()` for function calls
- Dependencies use **version catalog** accessors: `implementation(libs.core.ktx)`
- Plugins use **alias**: `alias(libs.plugins.kotlin.android)`
- Never hardcode version strings in build files — always use `libs.versions.toml`
- Test deps: `testImplementation(libs.junit)`, `testImplementation(libs.mockk)`, etc.

#### Architecture
- **Data flow**: `Fragment → ViewModel → Repository → DAO → Room DB`
- **Never** call DAOs directly from Fragments or ViewModels — always go through Repository
- Repositories take DAOs as constructor params (injected via Hilt `RepositoryModule`)
- ViewModels lazily initialize repositories from `FinancialDB` today; migration to constructor injection is tracked in CHRIS-231
- Use `activityViewModels()` for ViewModels shared between fragments and MainActivity

#### Dependency Injection (Hilt)
- DI graph lives in `di/` — `DatabaseModule` (provides `@Singleton FinancialDB` + DAOs) and `RepositoryModule` (provides repositories)
- Application class `FinanControlApp` is `@HiltAndroidApp`; new Activities/Fragments needing injection use `@AndroidEntryPoint`
- New ViewModels use `@HiltViewModel` with `@Inject constructor(...)`; obtain them via `viewModels()`/`activityViewModels()`
- Prefer Hilt injection over `FinancialDB.getAppDataBase(context)` — the manual singleton is `@Deprecated`
- Hilt uses **kapt** (consistent with Room); `kapt { correctErrorTypes = true }` is required

#### Kotlin
- Use `ViewBinding.bind(view)` — never `inflate()`
- Coroutines: `viewModelScope.launch(dispatcher)` with injectable dispatcher for testing
- Database singleton: `FinancialDB.getAppDataBase(context)`
- Dialogs communicate results via listener interfaces on `MainActivity`
- New adapters → `data/adapter/`, new dialogs → `data/dialog/`
- New strings must be added to both `values/strings.xml` and `values-es/strings.xml`
- Always use string resources, never hardcoded strings

#### Signing
- Signing variables: `myKeystorePassword`, `myKeyAlias`, `myKeyPassword`, `myKeystoreFile`, `canSign`

#### Testing (MockK + Page Object Pattern)
- **Page Objects** in `test/page/` encapsulate mock setup, SUT creation, stubs, and verifications
- Use `mockk(relaxed = true)` for mocks, `coEvery`/`coVerify` for suspend functions, `every`/`verify` for regular
- ViewModel testability: `@VisibleForTesting internal fun setTestRepository()` and `setTestDispatcher()`
- Use `InstantTaskExecutorRule` for LiveData, `StandardTestDispatcher` + `advanceUntilIdle()` for coroutines
- Test class naming: `[ClassUnderTest]Test`, Page Object: `[ClassUnderTest]Page`
- Test method naming: backtick-enclosed descriptive names
- Run tests with: `./gradlew testDebugUnitTest`

### Environment Setup

Before running any Gradle commands, ensure these environment variables are set:

```bash
export ANDROID_HOME="$HOME/Android/Sdk"
export JAVA_HOME="$HOME/.local/share/android-studio/jbr"
export PATH="$ANDROID_HOME/platform-tools:$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
```

Also ensure `local.properties` exists at project root:
```properties
sdk.dir=/home/locotito-linux/Android/Sdk
```

These should be configured in `~/.bashrc` for persistence across terminal sessions.

### Build Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `./gradlew assembleDebug` | Build debug APK |
| `./gradlew testDebugUnitTest` | Run all unit tests |
| `./gradlew clean testDebugUnitTest` | Clean + run tests (use after adding new test files) |
| `./gradlew compileDebugKotlin` | Compile production code only |
| `./gradlew compileDebugUnitTestKotlin` | Compile test code only |

> ⚠️ First build after adding test dependencies will download libraries (MockK, etc.) and may take 1-2 minutes.
> ⚠️ After adding new test source files, always run `clean` first — Gradle incremental build may skip new test source sets.
> ⚠️ Long-running builds may time out in some shell environments; use `nohup ./gradlew ... > /tmp/build.log 2>&1 &disown` to run in background.
